# Sixteen tabs overflow the strip (Rust's chips: an icon, the name,
# `󰅖`, three cells between). The strip ends on the active tab with
# the `󰐕` after it and the pager on the right, ` ‹ 4/4 › ` — the last
# page of four (`ui/stepper.zig`), the ` ⋯ ` that opens the buffer
# picker after it. The wheel over the strip scrolls it a tab at a time,
# back to the first tab and forward again; Ctrl+Tab wraps to the first
# tab and reveals it.
# The strip's right cluster paints an AI chip for a `claude` / `codex`
# found on PATH, which would cost the strip three cells on a machine
# that has one; nothing here spawns, so PATH is empty and the layout
# is the same everywhere.
# env: PATH=
write alpha.zig "const alpha = 1;\n"
write t1.txt "t1\n"
write t2.txt "t2\n"
write t3.txt "t3\n"
write t4.txt "t4\n"
write t5.txt "t5\n"
write t6.txt "t6\n"
write t7.txt "t7\n"
write t8.txt "t8\n"
write t9.txt "t9\n"
write t10.txt "t10\n"
write t11.txt "t11\n"
write t12.txt "t12\n"
write t13.txt "t13\n"
write t14.txt "t14\n"
write t15.txt "t15\n"
open alpha.zig
open t1.txt
open t2.txt
open t3.txt
open t4.txt
open t5.txt
open t6.txt
open t7.txt
open t8.txt
open t9.txt
open t10.txt
open t11.txt
open t12.txt
open t13.txt
open t14.txt
open t15.txt
expect screen contains "t15.txt 󰅖   󰐕"
expect screen contains "‹ 4/4 ›"
expect screen lacks "󰅁  󰅂"
expect screen lacks "alpha.zig 󰅖   󰈙 t1.txt"
scroll 60 1 up
expect screen lacks "t15.txt 󰅖   󰐕"
# One tab further left: the window was t12…t15, so it is now t11…t14.
expect screen contains "t11.txt 󰅖"
scroll 60 1 up
scroll 60 1 up
scroll 60 1 up
scroll 60 1 up
scroll 60 1 up
scroll 60 1 up
scroll 60 1 up
scroll 60 1 up
scroll 60 1 up
scroll 60 1 up
scroll 60 1 up
expect screen contains "  alpha.zig 󰅖   󰈙 t1.txt 󰅖"
scroll 60 1 down
expect screen lacks "alpha.zig 󰅖   󰈙 t1.txt"
expect screen contains "󰐕"
key ctrl+tab
expect screen contains "alpha.zig"
